1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:03,900
Hey! Usopp! Are you there?

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,600
Where did you run out to? Come back!

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,420
Hey! Usopp!

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,140
I'll be up here for sure.

5
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:16,080
Where are you hiding?

6
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,240
Are you in there? Usopp!

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,560
Seriously, I just saw him!

8
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,200
Hey, they're calling you. No, I can't.

9
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:26,600
It's too soon.

10
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,940
Stop playing hide-and-seek!

11
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,760
Get out here or I'll kick your ass!

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Kick your ass!

13
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:39,017
Hey, do you know where
it was up at Sniper King?

14
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,571
You're his friend, right?

15
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:42,780
Oh, uh, no need to fear.

16
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,156
He took a different boat and
went on ahead by himself.

17
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:47,840
But why?

18
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:49,577
That doesn't make sense.

19
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,157
The Mary's his ship, right?

20
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,780
You gotta be kidding me.

21
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:56,727
If they haven't figured it out
yet, then what's it gonna take?

22
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:00,040
Not here, either.

23
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,640
What the heck is going on?

24
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,440
I checked everywhere.

25
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,877
Looks like we're the
only ones on the ship.

26
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,254
That's pretty strange.

27
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:14,952
The Mary didn't sail itself here, did it?

28
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:16,570
Of course not.

29
00:01:16,653 --> 00:01:18,020
Someone was calling us.

30
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:19,780
The whole crew heard it.

31
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,960
And you don't know who it was? No.

32
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:24,057
Just a voice beckoning us to the sea.

33
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:25,197
Come on, you guys.

34
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,757
The answer here is obvious.

35
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:29,217
I'm telling you, that was
Mary's voice we heard.

36
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:30,130
Huh?

37
00:01:30,213 --> 00:01:31,180
You think so?

38
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,320
Mary, come on!

39
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,617
Say something else!

40
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,524
I think we'd know by now
if the ship could talk.

41
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:43,836
You know, as ridiculous as it may
sound, I was thinking the same thing.

42
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,620
But there's no way, right?

43
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,399
That's impossible.

44
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,020
Hey, look, there's a ship coming! What?

45
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,400
Who is it?

46
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,900
I can see the Straw Hat!

47
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,800
I knew they'd make it!

48
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:09,860
I just knew it!

49
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,760
It's a galley log company ship.

50
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:16,197
I thought they were done for when
they went out during Aqualaguna!

51
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,520
Forget Aqualaguna!

52
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,420
They survived Enies Lobby!

53
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,960
Ha-ha-ha! Ahoy!

54
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:25,540
What's up, Icebox?

55
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,240
Nice surprise, huh?

56
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,340
Nico Robin survived.

57
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:35,450
Hmm.

58
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,960
They pulled it off after all.

59
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,671
They took on the world government and won.

60
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,460
Ha-ha-ha! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

61
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,760
They lost it all, and then
they brought it all back.

62
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:07,410
Barry!

63
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,620
Their ship! It's breaking!

64
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,557
Hey, why is it falling
apart all of a sudden?

65
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:16,377
There's nothing sudden about it.

66
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,342
We all knew this was inevitable.

67
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,380
They told us, right?

68
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:24,397
Before we left, they said
Mary was unfit to sail.

69
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,860
Yeah, but...

70
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,480
What happened to you, Mary?

71
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:34,680
Ice Puffs, help!

72
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,139
Mary's in trouble!

73
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,613
Can't you do something?

74
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:39,340
You got here just in time!

75
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,977
You're all shipwrights, aren't you?

76
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:42,001
I'm begging you!

77
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:43,394
Don't let her die now!

78
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,877
Mary's more than just a ship!

79
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,377
She's a member of our crew!

80
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:49,537
If it wasn't for her, we all
would have died back there!

81
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,240
So come on, do something!

82
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,769
She's fought hard for you.

83
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,380
But it's time to let her rest.

84
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:06,462
Besides, I've already done
everything that I can.

85
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,680
What's that noise?

86
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,400
Someone on Scrap Island?

87
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:28,980
Wait a second.

88
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:31,040
This is the Strawhead ship.

89
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,900
Aqua Laguna did quite a number on it.

90
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,180
It's a wreck.

91
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,980
No, this is from long before that.

92
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,900
I want to sail.

93
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,940
What was that voice?

94
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:57,180
I want to sail one last time.

95
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,020
What am I doing?

96
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:27,745
There's no hope for this ship.

97
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,080
Mr. Iceberg!

98
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,480
You gotta get out of there!

99
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,700
Another tidal wave's about to hit!

100
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,140
Thank you.

101
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:10,140
Oh, I'm ready, you ship.

102
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,437
The weather's still too rough out there.

103
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,780
Then I'll go alone.

104
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:17,180
Are you kidding? No,
no. We'll go with you!

105
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:20,980
This is a miracle.

106
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,586
There's no other word for it.

107
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:29,000
The miracle of a ship that's gone beyond
its limits to see you one last time.

108
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:34,237
As you know, I've been a
shipwright for many years.

109
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:37,620
But I've never seen a ship
as incredible as this one.

110
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,020
It's lived a wonderful life.

111
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:51,077
Let's go back, everyone?

112
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:57,560
Back to the seas of adventure!

113
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,470
Mary!

114
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,120
I came to get you

115
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:22,240
I understand.

116
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,160
Well, guys, you ready?

117
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:24,870
Yeah.

118
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:36,340
Mary, I know the floor of the
sea is a dark and lonely place,

119
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,049
but don't worry, we're
here to see you off.

120
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:47,507
I'm sure you wish you was here, but it's
probably best that Usopp isn't around.

121
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:50,040
I don't know if you can take this.

122
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:51,400
Well, is that true?

123
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,280
Of course it isn't.

124
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,235
We must all say our farewells someday.

125
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,295
Every man knows that.

126
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:00,340
We must hold back our tears.

127
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:07,860
Luffy knows what has to be done.

128
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:43,600
Thank you for carrying us for
so long and for so far, Barry.

129
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,640
Snow?

130
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:10,660
The real Carabelle!

131
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:11,880
Yeah!

132
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:19,860
Now the going Mary has
everything she can possibly need!

133
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:24,280
Cheers to a new ship and a new Gourmet!

134
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,588
Look at all the damage
you did to poor Mary!

135
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,075
The crew has to take care of its ship!

136
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,760
And don't you forget it!

137
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,660
Right, we're sorry!

138
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:46,935
Hey, Luffy, what's so loud down there?

139
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,080
Cannon firing practice!

140
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:51,345
Then it's not going very well.

141
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,206
Let the expert aim the thing!

142
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:57,690
Blossom!

143
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,660
You hit that on the first try!

144
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,880
Uh, whatcha think?

145
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,611
So are you impressed yet?

146
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:29,020
I'm going to the Grand
Line to find the all-blue.

147
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:32,340
I'm going to be King of the Pirates.

148
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,980
The world's best swordsman.

149
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,780
I'm going so I can draw
a map of the whole world.

150
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:42,900
I'm going to be a brave
warrior of the sea.

151
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:47,100
And now, to the Grand Line!

152
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:00,167
The entrance to the
Grand Line is a mountain!

153
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:19,180
We made it!

154
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,680
I can see it!

155
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,237
This is the greatest
sea in the whole world!

156
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,740
The Grand Law!

157
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,060
Let's go!

158
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:53,217
Ha ha ha!

159
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:54,477
We're flying!

160
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:58,089
Don't bother looking back, cause
we're going straight ahead!

161
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,497
I'm afraid there's
nowhere left for me to go.

162
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:11,017
And for that matter, there's no
place for me to return to either.

163
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,837
So I've decided to stay here with you.

164
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,720
I see your problem.

165
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,685
Guess there's no other choice.

166
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:17,650
Welcome.

167
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:18,650
Hooray!

168
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,520
Trust me, I'm a navigator, aren't I?

169
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:23,100
We're flying!

170
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,310
Yeah!

171
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,520
We're headed to the sky!

172
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:33,140
There it is!

173
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,920
Sky Island!

174
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,920
I can't believe it.

175
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,077
I can't

176
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:53,097
believe

177
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:59,300
it.

178
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,750
No!

179
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:57,720
I'm sorry.

180
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:08,960
I wanted to carry everyone
just a little bit further.

181
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:13,400
I had so much fun.

182
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:16,280
I wish our adventures would never end.

183
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,750
Mary!

184
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,360
Who is that?

185
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,980
But I'm sorry, I... No, Mary!

186
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:30,320
If anyone should apologize,
it's us, not you!

187
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,120
I'm no good at steering!

188
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:35,360
I ran you into icebergs
and all kinds of stuff!

189
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,860
I took bad care of you
and ripped your sails!

190
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,500
Zoro and Sanji are idiots too.

191
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:46,449
They were breaking your
stuff all the time.

192
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,200
Usopp tried to fix you, but
he wasn't any good at it.

193
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,680
We all know that.

194
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,440
If anyone sorry, it's us.

195
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,280
I don't mind.

196
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:03,760
I was happy.

197
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,940
I know you always treated me with love.

198
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:12,660
Thank you.

199
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,700
Even if the time we
spent together was short,

200
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:27,280
I'm glad that I could spend it with you.

201
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,140
Mary!
